---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import Fill from '../components/Fill.astro';
import { OWNER } from '../config/legal';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Advertising and sponsorship"
  description="Who pays B2BRated today, and the rules that will apply to every paid placement, lead and badge."
  path="/advertising-disclosure"
>
  <h2>Today</h2>
  <p>
    No vendor pays us. The site has no affiliate links, no sponsored placements, no ads and no paid listings. Every
    product appears because it meets the written criteria for its category.
  </p>

  <h2>How we expect to earn money</h2>
  <p>
    We plan to charge vendors for tools and services: claimed and maintained profiles, lead requests that a buyer sends
    to a vendor, labelled sponsored placements, ad slots and licences to display badges a product has earned. We may
    also earn affiliate commissions. Nothing on this list has started.
  </p>

  <h2>Rules that apply from the first payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Payment never changes a product's score, its position in the ranked list or whether it is listed.</li>
    <li>
      Sponsored products sit in a separate block marked "Sponsored", with a short explanation of what that means. They
      are never mixed into the ranked list.
    </li>
    <li>Ads are marked "Ad" next to the ad itself, not only at the bottom of the page.</li>
    <li>
      A link that earns us a commission carries the words "Affiliate link: we earn a commission if you buy" next to it,
      before you click.
    </li>
    <li>
      Each category page names every vendor on the page that pays us, and what it pays for. The count on the
      <a href="/transparency">transparency page</a> comes from the same data.
    </li>
    <li>
      Badges and awards come from published criteria that anyone can check. A vendor can pay to display a badge it
      earned. It cannot pay to earn one.
    </li>
    <li>
      Lead requests are sent only to the vendor you choose, after you agree to that on the form. We do not pass your
      details to anyone you did not pick.
    </li>
    <li>We do not accept payment for reviews, or for a particular rating.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If a rule here is broken</h2>
  <p>
    Tell us at <Fill value={OWNER.email} label="contact email" />. We will fix the page and say what changed.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
